    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0070" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/198: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-14T23:00:00-04:00">June 14, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4729. We welcome the information set forth in your Comea 61 (Embassy’s 4655 of
                    June 10).<anchor n="31" xml:id="d41-f1"/> With respect to the question of
                    consultation with other Allied Governments, we very much hope for definite
                    recommendations at an early date, particularly in view of the developments
                    reported in Schoenfeld’s Nater [<hi rendition="#italic">Neter</hi>] 11, June 10,
                    4 p.m. Department’s views on consultation were explained in its 374T of May 10,
                    9 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d41-f2"/> and its instruction 4067 of May
                        13.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d41-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please keep Schoenfeld as well as the Department fully informed of all
                    developments on this subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d41-f1" n="31" xml:id="d41-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref target="#pg233">p. 233</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d41-f2" n="32" xml:id="d41-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported on the British Embassy’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of April 15, <ref target="#pg54">p. 54</ref>, and the
                    Department’s reply of May 9, <ref target="#pg56">p. 56</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d41-f3" n="33" xml:id="d41-f3-content">
